WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:05.270
We reached a new high or a new low, depending
on your perspective in the United States in

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.720
the growth of [inaudible] income

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:14.040
inequality and the 400 richest Americans are
now paying a lower total tax rate, federal,

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.789
state, and local than any other income group.

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:20.810
This is based on 2018 data, which has now
been analyzed.

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:25.759
There is a really good piece in the New York
times by David Lennart Leonhard.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:30.039
I'm not exactly sure how he pronounces his
last name, uh, about this.

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:36.149
And when you look at the, uh, the data and
the visualizations of the data back in 1950,

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:42.440
the top 400 richest Americans paid the most
in taxes when you combined federal, state

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:49.820
and local 50 years later, even in the year
2000, the richest 400 didn't pay the highest

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:54.480
total rates, but it was still a much higher
rate than the poor and middle class.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.620
You still had the very rich but not quite
as rich as the richness.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.870
400 paying slightly higher rates than the
richest 400.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.251
But no question that those richest 400 were
paying a higher total rate federal, state

00:01:06.251 --> 00:01:08.890
and local than lower income earners.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:17.180
And then last year in 2018 the richest 400
actually paid the lowest total rate of any

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:18.180
income group.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.490
Now you might see that.

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:22.880
You might hear me say this and wonder how
is that possible?

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.960
Because when you look at the federal tax brackets
for 2018 for example, uh, we see that the

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:36.110
tax bracket is highest at 37% for those earning
over $500,000.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:40.070
But what you need to understand is that is
that we're talking here about a group [inaudible]

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:48.230
400 that is so far above the entryway to that
top bracket of 500,000 that they have so many

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:55.430
different mechanisms for deductions and loopholes
and exclusions and the moving around of money

00:01:55.430 --> 00:02:02.189
on paper that they now are paying the lowest
combined federal, state and local rate of

00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:03.509
any income group.

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:10.390
Now let's discuss a common argument that we
hear from the American right wing, which is,

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:16.830
listen, whatever rules you pass, whatever
tax law you change, the rich will figure out

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.810
a way to avoid those taxes.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.140
So what's the point?

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.000
They'll get better accountants.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.510
They will somehow figure out a way to avoid
those taxes.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.560
This is completely untrue.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.710
Number one, look at the historical numbers
I just showed you, right?

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:38.030
I mean, the rich have historically not avoided
all taxes paid the lowest rates they used

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.460
to pay more than lower income brackets.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.160
So historically we know that that argument
is bogus.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.950
Number two, Oh, and I should mention, we're
talking about the very, very rich here.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:56.140
We're talking about the richest 400 the richest
0.1% we are not talking about a doctor making

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:58.060
$300,000 okay?

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.510
That's not who we're talking about here.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:02.780
And it's important to understand that there
is a distinction here.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:08.730
Number two, historically attempt to collect
more taxes have worked.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:13.070
We know that when we look at historical tax
collections, and number three, if the rich

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:17.060
could just avoid any new taxes, why would
they work so hard?

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:24.510
Why would they spend so much time and money
and political capital fighting new taxes?

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.310
Because they know that they would be affected
by them.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:29.470
So that argument is a completely bogus and
ridiculous argument.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:34.130
These are basically just choices to be made
by societies.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:39.680
And the trick of course, by the very rich
and corporations and the upper class is to

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.820
foam that class warfare down below.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:48.240
This has always been the technique you hear
from some brainwashed right wingers that the

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:54.760
left of the middle class and the lower middle
class, the poor are the ones fighting and

00:03:54.760 --> 00:04:01.030
pushing, you know, race warfare, class warfare,
that if it weren't for them, then everything

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:03.070
would just be completely fine.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:08.610
But understand that this is a technique that
the very rich use look at the battle between

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:14.760
American born restaurant and agricultural
workers and so-called illegals from Latin

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.690
America coming here to steal your jobs.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:23.840
That is a battle that corporate America and
the super rich and the upper class want you

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:25.090
to be having.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:26.090
Why?

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:31.710
Because if you as an American born restaurant
worker are fighting against the idea of some

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:37.889
hardworking Mexican dad coming here to quote,
steal your job, uh, you are not going to be

00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:42.500
fighting the actual people that are deciding
policy and that are controlling the system

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:44.139
and maintaining the status quo.

00:04:44.139 --> 00:04:45.139
It is by design.

00:04:45.139 --> 00:04:51.419
A another example, while the super rich and
corporate media talk about millennials are

00:04:51.419 --> 00:04:57.449
lazy and this and that, it's the super rich
who win by being ignored.

00:04:57.449 --> 00:05:03.330
They take the focus off of the fact that the
student loan burden on millennials is astronomical.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:10.749
They remove any discussion whatsoever of how
the ratio between the cost of college and

00:05:10.749 --> 00:05:16.159
the salary one expects to earn has fallen
completely out of whack compared to what it

00:05:16.159 --> 00:05:18.620
was 30 40 years ago.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:25.240
This is all by design and it is really important
that we not allow that to distract us from

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:29.580
what actually needs to be done when it comes
to policy because when we're having the wrong

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.030
debate, they win.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:34.569
That's the, the sick genius of it.

00:05:34.569 --> 00:05:37.680
They don't care who wins these false debates,
right?

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:42.830
If you're a big corporation and you benefit
from cheap labor and deregulation of labor

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:49.889
and all of this stuff, do you care whether
the quote, illegals win against the poor American

00:05:49.889 --> 00:05:54.419
born white people in the battle around who's
going to steal who's job?

00:05:54.419 --> 00:05:55.419
No.

00:05:55.419 --> 00:05:59.449
The fact that it's a battle that is even going
on means that you win.

00:05:59.449 --> 00:06:03.180
And this is what we fundamentally have to
understand when we look at these numbers.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:10.139
So inequality, uh, certainly getting worse
and worse, partially on the back of a tax

00:06:10.139 --> 00:06:15.999
code that now has the richest 400 Americans
in the lowest total tax bracket.

00:06:15.999 --> 00:06:16.569
When you combine federal, state, and local.

